            <h2 class="section-title">Photocell Configurations</h2>
            <p>Royce Thompson photocells are available in a number of configurations, with light level detection or Part Night operation, to meet the various needs of the street and amenity lighting market, including:</p>
            <h3 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 30px;">One Part NEMA photocell</h3>
            <p>For controlling photocell switching, the Royce Thompson photocell is housed in a single enclosure, with base fitting to NEMA socket as specified.</p>
            <p>This photocell is ideal for applications where a simple on/off control is required, and where the photocell is mounted on a pole or mast arm.</p>
            <h3 style="font-size: 16pt; margin-top: 30px;">One Part Microprocessor photocell</h3>
            <p>This photocell is housed in a single enclosure, with base fitting to NEMA socket as specified. It features microprocessor technology for advanced control and monitoring capabilities.</p>
            <p>This photocell is ideal for applications where more sophisticated control is required, such as dimming or monitoring.</p>
